WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.920
One thing we love as teachers

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.860
is to know if our students have

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.860
really understood concepts.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.200
And how can we do that?

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.360
By giving them quizzes and assignments;

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.180
That's right!

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.040
and Google Classroom has made that really easy!

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.760
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.220
On your Google Classroom dashboard,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.660
you can pick the Class

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.200
you’d like to add questions

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.420
or assignments to.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.240
And then you can head over

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.580
to the ClassWork section!

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.880
Once you click on CREATE,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.680
you will see 3 options

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.960
that will help you assess

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.720
the understanding level of students.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.020
You could give the students Long Form Assignments,

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.660
or graded quizzes,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.140
or you could also ask them

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.820
just one simple question.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.760
Let’s look at the options one by one.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.300
If you wish to give your students an assignment,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.560
or some task,

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.400
the first option works best.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.540
For instance,

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.140
you may want to ask your students

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.940
“What does the word LINEAR mean?

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.760
Explain using text and images”.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.700
So we just have to click on Create,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.180
and select ‘Assignment’.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.820
First, you will need to enter some basic information.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:10.860
After that,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.100
you can add a file from Google Drive.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.420
Google Drive is a place where

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.740
you can store your files on remote servers,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.020
and NOT on your local machine or laptop.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.420
The data here is completely safe

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.640
and no one can really access your files

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.260
unless you give anyone

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.980
the permission to do so!

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.000
You can access your files whenever you feel like.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.120
Let’s now add a document you want to share!

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.120
Here it is!

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.740
At this point,

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.060
Google Classroom gives you an interesting option.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.760
It asks you

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.120
“what it is that

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.000
you’d want your students to do with this file?”

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.840
Should they be able to just view it?

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:49.800
Can all students edit your same file?

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.440
Or automatically make a

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.440
different copy for each student.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:54.820
You can then select

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.960
the most appropriate option for yourself....

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.360
select the details on the right….

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.280
and click ‘Assign’.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.740
How will the students see it?

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.780
Let’s move to the student view now!

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.120
The students will then be able to see

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.880
the assignment on their dashboard.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.320
After they click on it,

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.320
they will see this screen.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.060
The students will now be able to see

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.320
the copy created for them by you.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:18.900
They can click on it,

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.020
and write their answer in the same file.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.220
If there is something else

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.780
the students have to share,

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.620
they can add their work using the

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.460
Add or Create option they see here.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.740
After the student is done,

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.580
they can then click on Turn in

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.660
to submit their work.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.460
It’ll ask the students for the confirmation,

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.680
and then it’s done!

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.960
If the student submits it by mistake

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.040
or if the student feels like adding

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.420
or editing the assignment,

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.980
the student can also unsubmit it

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.740
and then submit it again

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.880
Let’s switch back to the teacher view!

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.260
We will look at the second option of

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.400
“Quiz Assignment” in much greater detail

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.739
in the next lesson.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.040
For now

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.900
let’s look at how you can simply add

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.640
a SINGLE question to the class,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.500
which is the third option!

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.280
Clicking on QUESTION

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.820
will get you to this page.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.280
Note that this is used only

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.560
if you want to add a SINGLE question

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.160
and not a series of questions.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.000
You can then enter your question,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.960
and add some instructions with it…

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.380
You can then pick if

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.620
it’s a short answer question

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.080
or a multiple choice.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.200
Let’s pick multiple choice,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.480
and add 4 options.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.820
If you want your students to visit

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.400
a particular link or a youtube video,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.280
you can do that by clicking on Add.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.940
And you can also add documents

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.580
or presentations for their reference,

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.280
using the other options.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.600
You can then decide

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.740
if you wish to share it with all students,

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.820
or just a few.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.580
You could either assign marks

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.120
or keep it ungraded,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.180
and have a due date if required.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.820
And then you should select which topic

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.520
this question is a part of!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.860
And then you can click on ASK!

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.180
Your question is now Live

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.680
and your students will see it

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.000
on their dashboards.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.660
Alright, switching to the student view now!

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.580
Students will see the question like this.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.520
They can select the correct answer,

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.060
and click on ‘Turn In’.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.580
Once the student answers the question,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.420
she will also be able to see the class summary.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.740
Note that teachers could use this

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.960
‘single question option’ in different ways.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.300
Some teachers use it to take a poll,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.180
or may be to support the social

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.260
and emotional well-being

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.680
of students as well.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.560
Pretty easy wasn’t it?

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.680
But what if you want to ask your students

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.100
to appear for a quiz

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.480
that has say 10 or 15 questions?

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.960
You can then select the Quiz Assignment option

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.000
you see here!

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.300
We will explore this option in the next video!

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:47.920
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.920
[ YouTube Learning ]

